1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,608
In twenty twenty-six,

2
00:00:01,608 --> 00:00:04,290
the safest pickup truck in America,

3
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:07,967
according to the Insurance Institute for Highway

4
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,495
Safety, was the Tesla Cybertruck.

5
00:00:10,675 --> 00:00:11,878
The Ford F-150,

6
00:00:11,878 --> 00:00:15,167
the Ram fifteen hundred and the Chevrolet

7
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:18,938
Silverado all earned the lowest possible rating

8
00:00:18,938 --> 00:00:21,746
in one of the institute's key crash

9
00:00:21,746 --> 00:00:22,227
tests.

10
00:00:22,407 --> 00:00:24,714
And not a single small pickup won

11
00:00:24,714 --> 00:00:25,762
a safety award.

12
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:28,565
These are the truck safety ratings nobody

13
00:00:28,565 --> 00:00:29,332
talks about.

14
00:00:29,682 --> 00:00:32,295
Most truck buyers assume a big truck

15
00:00:32,295 --> 00:00:33,456
is a safe truck.

16
00:00:33,636 --> 00:00:34,573
It is tall,

17
00:00:34,573 --> 00:00:35,595
it is heavy,

18
00:00:35,595 --> 00:00:37,895
and in a crash with a small

19
00:00:37,895 --> 00:00:39,685
car, it usually wins.

20
00:00:39,865 --> 00:00:41,443
That part is true.

21
00:00:41,623 --> 00:00:43,919
But the people who crash test vehicles

22
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:46,093
for a living look at something else.

23
00:00:46,273 --> 00:00:48,149
They look at who is sitting in

24
00:00:48,149 --> 00:00:49,024
the back seat,

25
00:00:49,024 --> 00:00:51,400
how well the headlights work at night,

26
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,838
whether the truck stops itself before a

27
00:00:53,838 --> 00:00:56,151
crash, and what happens to the person

28
00:00:56,151 --> 00:00:57,651
standing in front of it.

29
00:00:58,001 --> 00:01:00,156
And when you measure those things,

30
00:01:00,156 --> 00:01:01,868
the results are surprising.

31
00:01:02,048 --> 00:01:05,225
The Insurance Institute for Highway Safety,

32
00:01:05,225 --> 00:01:06,259
known as IIHS,

33
00:01:06,259 --> 00:01:08,698
is funded by insurance companies,

34
00:01:08,698 --> 00:01:10,619
and its job is to find out

35
00:01:10,619 --> 00:01:13,426
which vehicles cost lives and money in

36
00:01:13,426 --> 00:01:14,018
crashes.

37
00:01:14,198 --> 00:01:16,529
Its tests are tougher than the federal

38
00:01:16,529 --> 00:01:18,737
minimum, and they change every year.

39
00:01:18,917 --> 00:01:20,450
In twenty twenty-six,

40
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:22,055
the bar went up again,

41
00:01:22,055 --> 00:01:24,536
and most pickups did not clear it.

42
00:01:24,886 --> 00:01:26,015
So in this video,

43
00:01:26,015 --> 00:01:28,470
we go through the safety ratings that

44
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:30,726
never appear in truck commercials.

45
00:01:30,906 --> 00:01:33,404
The back seat test that most pickups

46
00:01:33,404 --> 00:01:33,751
fail.

47
00:01:33,931 --> 00:01:35,568
The headlight scores.

48
00:01:35,748 --> 00:01:38,879
The automatic braking test with a motorcycle

49
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:40,160
and a semitrailer.

50
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:43,309
And the hood height research that explains

51
00:01:43,309 --> 00:01:45,784
why big trucks are so dangerous for

52
00:01:45,784 --> 00:01:46,632
pedestrians.

53
00:01:46,812 --> 00:01:48,932
There is a twist in every one,

54
00:01:48,932 --> 00:01:51,758
starting with which trucks actually won.

55
00:01:52,107 --> 00:01:55,324
As always, every rating here comes from

56
00:01:55,324 --> 00:01:56,891
a published source,

57
00:01:56,891 --> 00:02:00,521
mostly IIHS results reported by outlets like

58
00:02:00,521 --> 00:02:02,665
Pickup Truck and SUV Talk,

59
00:02:02,665 --> 00:02:05,552
GM Authority and Work Truck Online.

60
00:02:05,732 --> 00:02:07,938
The sources are in the description.

61
00:02:08,118 --> 00:02:09,592
And an important note.

62
00:02:09,772 --> 00:02:12,957
These ratings usually apply to a specific

63
00:02:12,957 --> 00:02:14,976
cab style and model years,

64
00:02:14,976 --> 00:02:17,539
so we will always say which ones.

65
00:02:17,719 --> 00:02:19,519
Let's start with the awards.

66
00:02:19,868 --> 00:02:21,825
One quick thing about how to read

67
00:02:21,825 --> 00:02:22,655
these ratings.

68
00:02:22,835 --> 00:02:24,729
IIHS uses four levels,

69
00:02:24,729 --> 00:02:27,827
good, acceptable, marginal and poor.

70
00:02:28,007 --> 00:02:29,296
Good is the top.

71
00:02:29,476 --> 00:02:30,672
Poor is the bottom.

72
00:02:30,852 --> 00:02:33,410
There is no partial credit for a

73
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:35,728
famous badge or a big engine.

74
00:02:35,908 --> 00:02:38,341
And because the tests get harder over

75
00:02:38,341 --> 00:02:40,643
time, a truck that earned good five

76
00:02:40,643 --> 00:02:42,879
years ago may not earn good today,

77
00:02:42,879 --> 00:02:45,509
even if nothing about the truck changed.

78
00:02:45,859 --> 00:02:47,711
On March twenty-fourth,

79
00:02:47,711 --> 00:02:51,656
twenty twenty-six, IIHS announced its first round

80
00:02:51,656 --> 00:02:54,474
of twenty twenty-six safety awards.

81
00:02:54,654 --> 00:02:56,839
Sixty-three vehicles qualified,

82
00:02:56,839 --> 00:02:59,447
up from forty-eight at the same point

83
00:02:59,447 --> 00:03:00,575
the year before.

84
00:03:00,755 --> 00:03:03,779
Forty-five earned Top Safety Pick Plus,

85
00:03:03,779 --> 00:03:05,174
the highest award,

86
00:03:05,174 --> 00:03:07,965
and eighteen earned Top Safety Pick.

87
00:03:08,145 --> 00:03:11,961
SUVs dominated, with thirty-five of the forty-five

88
00:03:11,961 --> 00:03:12,801
top awards.

89
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:14,184
And pickups?

90
00:03:14,364 --> 00:03:15,304
Only two.

91
00:03:15,484 --> 00:03:18,346
The Tesla Cybertruck crew cab earned Top

92
00:03:18,346 --> 00:03:19,563
Safety Pick Plus,

93
00:03:19,563 --> 00:03:21,638
the only truck to get the top

94
00:03:21,638 --> 00:03:22,067
award.

95
00:03:22,247 --> 00:03:24,816
The Toyota Tundra crew cab earned Top

96
00:03:24,816 --> 00:03:25,649
Safety Pick.

97
00:03:25,829 --> 00:03:26,502
That was it.

98
00:03:26,682 --> 00:03:28,972
No Ford, no Ram,

99
00:03:28,972 --> 00:03:31,976
no Chevrolet, no GMC.

100
00:03:32,156 --> 00:03:35,069
And no small pickup earned any award

101
00:03:35,069 --> 00:03:37,172
at all, according to IIHS.

102
00:03:37,352 --> 00:03:40,629
Out of the best-selling vehicles in America,

103
00:03:40,629 --> 00:03:42,565
almost none made the list.

104
00:03:42,915 --> 00:03:44,029
Why so few?

105
00:03:44,209 --> 00:03:46,125
Because the rules got stricter.

106
00:03:46,305 --> 00:03:47,945
For twenty twenty-six,

107
00:03:47,945 --> 00:03:50,705
a good rating in the updated moderate

108
00:03:50,705 --> 00:03:54,135
overlap front test became mandatory for either

109
00:03:54,135 --> 00:03:54,583
award.

110
00:03:54,763 --> 00:03:55,922
The year before,

111
00:03:55,922 --> 00:03:58,746
an acceptable rating was enough for Top

112
00:03:58,746 --> 00:03:59,616
Safety Pick.

113
00:03:59,796 --> 00:04:02,512
Front crash prevention had to be standard

114
00:04:02,512 --> 00:04:03,174
equipment.

115
00:04:03,354 --> 00:04:04,950
And for the top award,

116
00:04:04,950 --> 00:04:07,345
a vehicle needed a good rating in

117
00:04:07,345 --> 00:04:09,377
pedestrian crash prevention,

118
00:04:09,377 --> 00:04:11,989
plus an acceptable or good rating in

119
00:04:11,989 --> 00:04:13,223
a brand-new test.

120
00:04:13,573 --> 00:04:16,738
That new test is called vehicle-to-vehicle front

121
00:04:16,738 --> 00:04:18,716
crash prevention two point oh.

122
00:04:18,896 --> 00:04:21,578
It replaced an older test IIHS dropped

123
00:04:21,578 --> 00:04:23,060
in twenty twenty-two,

124
00:04:23,060 --> 00:04:26,802
which only checked low-speed rear-end crashes against

125
00:04:26,802 --> 00:04:27,719
a car target.

126
00:04:27,899 --> 00:04:30,261
The new one runs at thirty-one,

127
00:04:30,261 --> 00:04:33,612
thirty-seven and forty-three miles per hour,

128
00:04:33,612 --> 00:04:36,659
and checks whether the vehicle can avoid

129
00:04:36,659 --> 00:04:39,173
or slow down for a passenger car,

130
00:04:39,173 --> 00:04:41,611
a motorcycle, and a semitrailer.

131
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,261
Here is the twist.

132
00:04:43,441 --> 00:04:45,124
Most vehicles passed it.

133
00:04:45,304 --> 00:04:48,194
IIHS says more than seventy percent of

134
00:04:48,194 --> 00:04:52,376
the eighty-five twenty twenty-five models tested earned

135
00:04:52,376 --> 00:04:53,820
acceptable or good,

136
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:57,014
and more than seventy-seven percent of the

137
00:04:57,014 --> 00:04:59,979
twenty twenty-six models tested so far.

138
00:05:00,159 --> 00:05:02,516
So the new test was not impossible.

139
00:05:02,696 --> 00:05:05,424
Most cars and SUVs handled it.

140
00:05:05,604 --> 00:05:08,241
Several of the most popular pickups did

141
00:05:08,241 --> 00:05:10,404
not, and that is where the story

142
00:05:10,404 --> 00:05:11,688
gets uncomfortable.

143
00:05:12,038 --> 00:05:14,073
Before we get to each truck,

144
00:05:14,073 --> 00:05:16,327
you need to know about the test

145
00:05:16,327 --> 00:05:17,999
that sank most of them,

146
00:05:17,999 --> 00:05:20,908
the updated moderate overlap front test.

147
00:05:21,088 --> 00:05:23,911
IIHS changed it after research found that

148
00:05:23,911 --> 00:05:25,150
in newer vehicles,

149
00:05:25,150 --> 00:05:28,318
belted rear-seat passengers face a higher risk

150
00:05:28,318 --> 00:05:30,659
of fatal injury than people in the

151
00:05:30,659 --> 00:05:34,033
front, according to Fleet and Insurance magazine.

152
00:05:34,213 --> 00:05:36,927
The front seats got better airbags and

153
00:05:36,927 --> 00:05:39,356
smarter seat belts over the years.

154
00:05:39,536 --> 00:05:41,637
The rear seats mostly did not.

155
00:05:41,988 --> 00:05:44,582
So the updated test puts a small

156
00:05:44,582 --> 00:05:47,988
dummy, about the size of a twelve-year-old

157
00:05:47,988 --> 00:05:49,366
or a small adult,

158
00:05:49,366 --> 00:05:52,204
in the rear seat behind the driver.

159
00:05:52,384 --> 00:05:54,792
And it measures what happens to that

160
00:05:54,792 --> 00:05:55,461
passenger.

161
00:05:55,641 --> 00:05:57,464
Does the head hit the front seat?

162
00:05:57,644 --> 00:06:00,106
Does the body slide under the lap

163
00:06:00,106 --> 00:06:02,717
belt, which IIHS calls submarining?

164
00:06:02,897 --> 00:06:04,762
Are the belt forces so high they

165
00:06:04,762 --> 00:06:05,753
injure the chest?

166
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:07,643
For a crew cab pickup,

167
00:06:07,643 --> 00:06:10,129
which is often a family vehicle,

168
00:06:10,129 --> 00:06:11,994
this test matters a lot.

169
00:06:12,344 --> 00:06:14,114
In twenty twenty-three,

170
00:06:14,114 --> 00:06:16,731
IIHS ran four big crew cab pickups

171
00:06:16,731 --> 00:06:20,041
through it, according to Work Truck Online.

172
00:06:20,221 --> 00:06:21,458
The Ford F-150,

173
00:06:21,458 --> 00:06:24,838
the Ram fifteen hundred and the Chevrolet

174
00:06:24,838 --> 00:06:28,301
Silverado fifteen hundred all earned poor.

175
00:06:28,481 --> 00:06:30,769
The Toyota Tundra earned marginal.

176
00:06:30,949 --> 00:06:33,329
All four protected the driver well.

177
00:06:33,509 --> 00:06:35,157
The problem was the back seat.

178
00:06:35,337 --> 00:06:37,117
In the F-150 and Ram,

179
00:06:37,117 --> 00:06:40,762
the rear dummy showed likely chest injuries

180
00:06:40,762 --> 00:06:42,965
and head or neck injuries.

181
00:06:43,315 --> 00:06:45,088
And here is the line from the

182
00:06:45,088 --> 00:06:46,861
IIHS president, David Harkey,

183
00:06:46,861 --> 00:06:49,061
that every truck family should hear.

184
00:06:49,241 --> 00:06:52,200
Quote, submarining was a problem for all

185
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:55,011
four pickups, and belt forces were too

186
00:06:55,011 --> 00:06:57,009
high in all but the Tundra.

187
00:06:57,189 --> 00:06:59,997
Submarining means the lap belt rides up

188
00:06:59,997 --> 00:07:02,229
from the hips onto the stomach,

189
00:07:02,229 --> 00:07:04,677
which can cause internal injuries.

190
00:07:04,857 --> 00:07:08,583
In all four of America's best-known full-size

191
00:07:08,583 --> 00:07:11,978
trucks, the rear passenger slid under the

192
00:07:11,978 --> 00:07:12,392
belt.

193
00:07:12,742 --> 00:07:14,274
Now the twist.

194
00:07:14,454 --> 00:07:17,163
These same trucks did well in the

195
00:07:17,163 --> 00:07:19,133
updated side crash test.

196
00:07:19,313 --> 00:07:21,728
Ram, Ford and Toyota earned good,

197
00:07:21,728 --> 00:07:24,363
and the Silverado earned acceptable.

198
00:07:24,543 --> 00:07:26,738
So these pickups are not weak trucks.

199
00:07:26,918 --> 00:07:29,116
They are strong trucks with rear seat

200
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:31,255
belts that were not designed for the

201
00:07:31,255 --> 00:07:31,968
newest test.

202
00:07:32,148 --> 00:07:35,241
Harkey said large pickups do not perform

203
00:07:35,241 --> 00:07:37,948
as well in the new moderate overlap

204
00:07:37,948 --> 00:07:40,732
evaluation as they do in the updated

205
00:07:40,732 --> 00:07:41,505
side test.

206
00:07:41,685 --> 00:07:43,357
The structure is fine.

207
00:07:43,537 --> 00:07:45,453
The back seat is the problem.

208
00:07:45,803 --> 00:07:48,435
So how do the best-selling trucks look

209
00:07:48,435 --> 00:07:49,889
in twenty twenty-six?

210
00:07:50,069 --> 00:07:53,808
Start with the Chevrolet Silverado fifteen hundred

211
00:07:53,808 --> 00:07:54,481
crew cab.

212
00:07:54,661 --> 00:07:58,120
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk's

213
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:00,541
summary of the IIHS ratings,

214
00:08:00,541 --> 00:08:04,951
it scored acceptable in pedestrian crash prevention

215
00:08:04,951 --> 00:08:06,334
and side impact,

216
00:08:06,334 --> 00:08:09,879
marginal in the small overlap front test,

217
00:08:09,879 --> 00:08:13,079
and poor in both the moderate overlap

218
00:08:13,079 --> 00:08:15,327
front test and headlights.

219
00:08:15,507 --> 00:08:18,224
The article called it the least safe

220
00:08:18,224 --> 00:08:21,846
full-size crew cab pickup for twenty twenty-six.

221
00:08:22,196 --> 00:08:24,737
And here is the detail that matters

222
00:08:24,737 --> 00:08:25,899
for used buyers.

223
00:08:26,079 --> 00:08:29,907
Those Silverado results apply to Silverado fifteen

224
00:08:29,907 --> 00:08:33,428
hundred crew cabs built since twenty nineteen.

225
00:08:33,608 --> 00:08:36,186
So this is not a one-year problem.

226
00:08:36,366 --> 00:08:38,618
It covers the whole current generation.

227
00:08:38,798 --> 00:08:41,427
And because the Sierra fifteen hundred shares

228
00:08:41,427 --> 00:08:43,354
its structure with the Silverado,

229
00:08:43,354 --> 00:08:45,749
buyers should check the GMC's own ratings

230
00:08:45,749 --> 00:08:48,086
too, rather than assume they are better.

231
00:08:48,436 --> 00:08:51,698
Next, the Ford F-150 crew cab.

232
00:08:51,878 --> 00:08:54,528
It scored good in the small overlap

233
00:08:54,528 --> 00:08:56,345
front test, side impact,

234
00:08:56,345 --> 00:08:58,465
pedestrian crash prevention,

235
00:08:58,465 --> 00:09:00,887
and headlights on some versions.

236
00:09:01,067 --> 00:09:03,537
But it scored poor in the moderate

237
00:09:03,537 --> 00:09:04,917
overlap front test,

238
00:09:04,917 --> 00:09:08,113
and poor in the new vehicle-to-vehicle crash

239
00:09:08,113 --> 00:09:09,276
prevention test.

240
00:09:09,456 --> 00:09:13,007
Those results apply to F-150s built after

241
00:09:13,007 --> 00:09:15,086
March twenty twenty-one.

242
00:09:15,266 --> 00:09:19,026
So America's best-selling truck failed the back

243
00:09:19,026 --> 00:09:22,146
seat test and the new automatic braking

244
00:09:22,146 --> 00:09:22,546
test.

245
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:25,392
Then the Ram fifteen hundred crew cab.

246
00:09:25,572 --> 00:09:28,340
Good in the small overlap front test,

247
00:09:28,340 --> 00:09:31,409
side impact, pedestrian crash prevention,

248
00:09:31,409 --> 00:09:33,803
and headlights on some versions.

249
00:09:33,983 --> 00:09:36,820
Poor in the moderate overlap front test,

250
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:40,508
and marginal in vehicle-to-vehicle crash prevention.

251
00:09:40,688 --> 00:09:43,395
Pickup Truck and SUV Talk called it

252
00:09:43,395 --> 00:09:46,644
the safest American pickup in the testing,

253
00:09:46,644 --> 00:09:50,125
with results that apply to twenty twenty-five

254
00:09:50,125 --> 00:09:52,368
and twenty twenty-six models.

255
00:09:52,718 --> 00:09:54,088
Here is the twist.

256
00:09:54,268 --> 00:09:57,026
The safest American pickup still earned a

257
00:09:57,026 --> 00:09:59,247
poor rating in the same back seat

258
00:09:59,247 --> 00:10:00,525
test as the others.

259
00:10:00,705 --> 00:10:02,676
So when an ad says a truck

260
00:10:02,676 --> 00:10:05,176
earned top marks in a crash test,

261
00:10:05,176 --> 00:10:06,313
ask which test.

262
00:10:06,493 --> 00:10:09,126
Every one of these trucks can honestly

263
00:10:09,126 --> 00:10:10,719
advertise good ratings.

264
00:10:10,899 --> 00:10:12,292
And every one of them,

265
00:10:12,292 --> 00:10:13,621
in its crew cab form,

266
00:10:13,621 --> 00:10:15,457
has a poor rating in the test

267
00:10:15,457 --> 00:10:18,243
that measures what happens to your passenger

268
00:10:18,243 --> 00:10:19,003
in the back.

269
00:10:19,353 --> 00:10:21,624
Now the Toyota Tundra crew cab,

270
00:10:21,624 --> 00:10:24,629
the only traditional pickup with an award

271
00:10:24,629 --> 00:10:26,168
in twenty twenty-six.

272
00:10:26,348 --> 00:10:29,342
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk,

273
00:10:29,342 --> 00:10:32,643
it scored good in the three crashworthiness

274
00:10:32,643 --> 00:10:35,715
tests, good or acceptable in headlights,

275
00:10:35,715 --> 00:10:39,246
and acceptable in pedestrian crash prevention.

276
00:10:39,426 --> 00:10:41,930
It also scored good on seat belt

277
00:10:41,930 --> 00:10:42,712
reminders.

278
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:45,126
That is a big improvement from the

279
00:10:45,126 --> 00:10:48,214
marginal rating in the twenty twenty-three back

280
00:10:48,214 --> 00:10:48,871
seat test.

281
00:10:49,221 --> 00:10:50,799
But here is the twist.

282
00:10:50,979 --> 00:10:53,255
The Tundra was a Top Safety Pick

283
00:10:53,255 --> 00:10:55,176
Plus in twenty twenty-five,

284
00:10:55,176 --> 00:10:57,594
and it dropped to plain Top Safety

285
00:10:57,594 --> 00:10:59,443
Pick in twenty twenty-six.

286
00:10:59,623 --> 00:11:01,625
Not because it got worse in a

287
00:11:01,625 --> 00:11:03,972
crash, but because it had no score

288
00:11:03,972 --> 00:11:07,562
in the new vehicle-to-vehicle crash prevention test,

289
00:11:07,562 --> 00:11:09,840
which the top award now requires.

290
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,669
The truck did not change.

291
00:11:11,849 --> 00:11:12,940
The rules did.

292
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,552
That is how fast the safety bar

293
00:11:15,552 --> 00:11:16,022
moves.

294
00:11:16,373 --> 00:11:19,194
And notice the difference from twenty twenty-three.

295
00:11:19,374 --> 00:11:22,141
Back then, IIHS said belt forces were

296
00:11:22,141 --> 00:11:24,535
too high in all four big pickups

297
00:11:24,535 --> 00:11:25,881
except the Tundra,

298
00:11:25,881 --> 00:11:28,574
and the Tundra's main issue was belt

299
00:11:28,574 --> 00:11:31,715
positioning that raised chest injury risk.

300
00:11:31,895 --> 00:11:35,230
Toyota's rear seat design was already closer

301
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:36,063
to passing.

302
00:11:36,243 --> 00:11:37,838
That is why it is the only

303
00:11:37,838 --> 00:11:39,924
traditional pickup that qualified.

304
00:11:40,104 --> 00:11:42,328
It is a reminder that rear seat

305
00:11:42,328 --> 00:11:44,194
safety is a design choice,

306
00:11:44,194 --> 00:11:46,849
not something only small cars can do.

307
00:11:47,199 --> 00:11:50,341
And then the Tesla Cybertruck crew cab,

308
00:11:50,341 --> 00:11:53,242
the only pickup with Top Safety Pick

309
00:11:53,242 --> 00:11:55,337
Plus in twenty twenty-six.

310
00:11:55,517 --> 00:11:58,899
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk,

311
00:11:58,899 --> 00:12:01,587
it scored good in all six award

312
00:12:01,587 --> 00:12:02,541
categories.

313
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:05,762
That includes the back seat test that

314
00:12:05,762 --> 00:12:08,720
the F-150, Ram and Silverado failed,

315
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:12,336
the headlights, pedestrian crash prevention,

316
00:12:12,336 --> 00:12:15,295
and the new vehicle-to-vehicle test.

317
00:12:15,645 --> 00:12:16,910
Here is the twist.

318
00:12:17,090 --> 00:12:20,222
The Cybertruck is the most polarizing truck

319
00:12:20,222 --> 00:12:21,095
on the road.

320
00:12:21,275 --> 00:12:23,823
It has been recalled for a glued-on

321
00:12:23,823 --> 00:12:26,442
panel, for an accelerator pedal pad,

322
00:12:26,442 --> 00:12:27,898
and for wheel studs,

323
00:12:27,898 --> 00:12:30,227
as we covered in earlier videos.

324
00:12:30,407 --> 00:12:32,776
And yet, in the crash tests that

325
00:12:32,776 --> 00:12:34,108
decide this award,

326
00:12:34,108 --> 00:12:36,107
it beat every other pickup.

327
00:12:36,287 --> 00:12:38,413
A truck can be controversial,

328
00:12:38,413 --> 00:12:41,418
recalled, and still be the best performer

329
00:12:41,418 --> 00:12:43,543
in the official safety tests.

330
00:12:43,723 --> 00:12:45,755
Those are simply different questions.

331
00:12:46,106 --> 00:12:47,417
It was not perfect.

332
00:12:47,597 --> 00:12:49,714
Outside the award categories,

333
00:12:49,714 --> 00:12:52,780
it scored marginal on seat belt reminders,

334
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:55,407
and acceptable on LATCH ease of use,

335
00:12:55,407 --> 00:12:57,451
the anchors for child seats,

336
00:12:57,451 --> 00:12:59,567
according to the same report.

337
00:12:59,747 --> 00:13:02,226
So if you install child seats often,

338
00:13:02,226 --> 00:13:04,636
or you want the strongest seat belt

339
00:13:04,636 --> 00:13:07,665
reminders, those details are worth checking.

340
00:13:07,845 --> 00:13:10,052
But on the tests that IIHS uses

341
00:13:10,052 --> 00:13:11,761
to decide its top award,

342
00:13:11,761 --> 00:13:13,256
no pickup did better.

343
00:13:13,606 --> 00:13:15,694
Let's stop and count what we have

344
00:13:15,694 --> 00:13:16,137
so far.

345
00:13:16,317 --> 00:13:19,720
Among the five best-known full-size crew cabs,

346
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:21,570
one earned the top award,

347
00:13:21,570 --> 00:13:23,642
one earned the second award,

348
00:13:23,642 --> 00:13:26,084
and three earned poor in the back

349
00:13:26,084 --> 00:13:26,824
seat test.

350
00:13:27,004 --> 00:13:29,275
And the two winners were the newest

351
00:13:29,275 --> 00:13:31,676
designs to be updated for the tougher

352
00:13:31,676 --> 00:13:32,065
tests.

353
00:13:32,245 --> 00:13:33,987
That pattern tells you something.

354
00:13:34,167 --> 00:13:37,145
Safety ratings reward recent engineering,

355
00:13:37,145 --> 00:13:39,396
so the model year can matter as

356
00:13:39,396 --> 00:13:40,703
much as the brand.

357
00:13:41,054 --> 00:13:43,328
Now the small and midsize pickups,

358
00:13:43,328 --> 00:13:46,004
which many families buy because they are

359
00:13:46,004 --> 00:13:47,811
easier to park and cheaper.

360
00:13:47,991 --> 00:13:49,954
In twenty twenty-three,

361
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:52,942
IIHS tested five small crew cabs in

362
00:13:52,942 --> 00:13:55,247
the updated back seat test.

363
00:13:55,427 --> 00:13:56,681
None earned good.

364
00:13:56,861 --> 00:13:59,229
The Nissan Frontier earned acceptable.

365
00:13:59,409 --> 00:14:01,603
The Ford Ranger earned marginal.

366
00:14:01,783 --> 00:14:03,892
And the Chevrolet Colorado,

367
00:14:03,892 --> 00:14:07,017
the Jeep Gladiator and the Toyota Tacoma

368
00:14:07,017 --> 00:14:08,267
all earned poor,

369
00:14:08,267 --> 00:14:10,688
according to Work Truck Online.

370
00:14:11,039 --> 00:14:12,292
The details matter.

371
00:14:12,472 --> 00:14:13,733
In the Colorado,

372
00:14:13,733 --> 00:14:15,938
Frontier, Ranger and Tacoma,

373
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:18,774
the rear dummy's head came too close

374
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:20,506
to the front seatback.

375
00:14:20,686 --> 00:14:23,379
The Gladiator's rear seat had no side

376
00:14:23,379 --> 00:14:26,289
curtain airbag, which raised the risk of

377
00:14:26,289 --> 00:14:28,036
injury in a hard impact.

378
00:14:28,216 --> 00:14:29,480
And in the Ranger,

379
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:32,218
the rear dummy submarined under the lap

380
00:14:32,218 --> 00:14:32,569
belt.

381
00:14:32,749 --> 00:14:35,227
IIHS president David Harkey said,

382
00:14:35,227 --> 00:14:38,531
quote, the rear seat belts need improvement.

383
00:14:38,881 --> 00:14:40,420
And in twenty twenty-six,

384
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:42,144
the problem was still there.

385
00:14:42,324 --> 00:14:43,927
On September third,

386
00:14:43,927 --> 00:14:48,060
twenty twenty-six, GM Authority reported that the

387
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:51,772
twenty twenty-six GMC Canyon crew cab earned

388
00:14:51,772 --> 00:14:55,652
marginal in the updated moderate overlap test.

389
00:14:55,832 --> 00:14:57,767
The structure was rated good,

390
00:14:57,767 --> 00:15:00,035
and the driver was well protected.

391
00:15:00,215 --> 00:15:03,114
But the rear passenger's head approached the

392
00:15:03,114 --> 00:15:06,408
front seatback, and measurements showed a moderate

393
00:15:06,408 --> 00:15:07,264
risk of head,

394
00:15:07,264 --> 00:15:08,713
neck and chest injury.

395
00:15:09,063 --> 00:15:11,391
Here is the twist for small truck

396
00:15:11,391 --> 00:15:11,885
buyers.

397
00:15:12,065 --> 00:15:15,117
Many people choose a smaller pickup because

398
00:15:15,117 --> 00:15:17,530
it feels safer and easier to drive

399
00:15:17,530 --> 00:15:19,588
than a giant full-size truck.

400
00:15:19,768 --> 00:15:21,568
But in the back seat test,

401
00:15:21,568 --> 00:15:23,645
the small crew cabs did not do

402
00:15:23,645 --> 00:15:25,376
better than the big ones.

403
00:15:25,556 --> 00:15:28,325
And IIHS listed no small pickup award

404
00:15:28,325 --> 00:15:30,571
winners for twenty twenty-six.

405
00:15:30,751 --> 00:15:32,972
If your kids ride in the back,

406
00:15:32,972 --> 00:15:35,784
a small truck is not automatically the

407
00:15:35,784 --> 00:15:36,672
safe choice.

408
00:15:37,022 --> 00:15:38,613
One important point,

409
00:15:38,613 --> 00:15:41,318
so nobody takes the wrong message.

410
00:15:41,498 --> 00:15:43,704
IIHS says the rear seat is still

411
00:15:43,704 --> 00:15:46,185
the safest place for young children,

412
00:15:46,185 --> 00:15:49,079
according to Fleet and Insurance magazine.

413
00:15:49,259 --> 00:15:51,894
Children in proper car seats should stay

414
00:15:51,894 --> 00:15:52,684
in the back.

415
00:15:52,864 --> 00:15:55,483
The test is about older kids and

416
00:15:55,483 --> 00:15:57,857
adults in regular seat belts.

417
00:15:58,037 --> 00:15:59,770
The answer is not to move kids

418
00:15:59,770 --> 00:16:00,521
to the front.

419
00:16:00,701 --> 00:16:02,951
The answer is to buy a truck

420
00:16:02,951 --> 00:16:04,800
that protects the back.

421
00:16:05,149 --> 00:16:07,853
Now the rating almost nobody checks,

422
00:16:07,853 --> 00:16:08,679
headlights.

423
00:16:08,859 --> 00:16:11,627
IIHS measures how far a vehicle's headlights

424
00:16:11,627 --> 00:16:14,332
light the road on straightaways and curves,

425
00:16:14,332 --> 00:16:16,220
and whether they create glare.

426
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:19,712
The Silverado fifteen hundred crew cab scored

427
00:16:19,712 --> 00:16:20,080
poor.

428
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:22,960
The F-150 and Ram scored good on

429
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:26,251
some versions and acceptable on others.

430
00:16:26,431 --> 00:16:28,323
And the word versions is the key.

431
00:16:28,503 --> 00:16:31,435
Headlight ratings often change by trim level,

432
00:16:31,435 --> 00:16:34,366
because different trims use different lights.

433
00:16:34,716 --> 00:16:35,889
Why does that matter?

434
00:16:36,069 --> 00:16:38,851
Trucks are often driven on rural roads

435
00:16:38,851 --> 00:16:41,120
at night, with no streetlights,

436
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:43,682
where seeing an animal or a stopped

437
00:16:43,682 --> 00:16:46,317
car a few seconds earlier can decide

438
00:16:46,317 --> 00:16:47,122
everything.

439
00:16:47,302 --> 00:16:50,140
A cheaper trim with weaker headlights may

440
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:52,078
be the more dangerous truck,

441
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:54,639
even if everything else is identical.

442
00:16:54,819 --> 00:16:56,268
So if you drive a lot at

443
00:16:56,268 --> 00:16:58,742
night, check the headlight rating for the

444
00:16:58,742 --> 00:17:00,311
exact trim you are buying.

445
00:17:00,660 --> 00:17:03,444
And the automatic braking test is the

446
00:17:03,444 --> 00:17:04,573
other surprise.

447
00:17:04,753 --> 00:17:07,084
The F-150 was poor in the new

448
00:17:07,084 --> 00:17:11,104
vehicle-to-vehicle test, and the Ram was marginal.

449
00:17:11,284 --> 00:17:14,043
The GMC Canyon was poor in standard

450
00:17:14,043 --> 00:17:18,220
front crash prevention in vehicle-to-vehicle testing,

451
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:20,270
according to GM Authority.

452
00:17:20,450 --> 00:17:23,856
Remember, this test includes a motorcycle and

453
00:17:23,856 --> 00:17:26,278
a semitrailer at highway speeds.

454
00:17:26,458 --> 00:17:28,800
If the system cannot see them in

455
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,556
time, the driver has to.

456
00:17:30,906 --> 00:17:32,979
And the last rating is about the

457
00:17:32,979 --> 00:17:34,598
person outside the truck.

458
00:17:34,778 --> 00:17:37,178
In November twenty twenty-three,

459
00:17:37,178 --> 00:17:40,251
IIHS published a study of nearly eighteen

460
00:17:40,251 --> 00:17:42,351
thousand pedestrian crashes,

461
00:17:42,351 --> 00:17:43,625
according to NPR.

462
00:17:43,805 --> 00:17:45,431
It found that pickups,

463
00:17:45,431 --> 00:17:48,164
SUVs and vans with hood heights above

464
00:17:48,164 --> 00:17:51,711
forty inches were forty-five percent more likely

465
00:17:51,711 --> 00:17:55,331
to cause pedestrian fatalities than vehicles with

466
00:17:55,331 --> 00:17:57,621
hoods of thirty inches or less.

467
00:17:57,971 --> 00:18:00,182
Among medium-height vehicles,

468
00:18:00,182 --> 00:18:02,621
between thirty and forty inches,

469
00:18:02,621 --> 00:18:03,916
those with blunt,

470
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:07,575
vertical front ends were twenty-six percent more

471
00:18:07,575 --> 00:18:11,233
likely to cause pedestrian fatalities than those

472
00:18:11,233 --> 00:18:12,681
with sloped fronts.

473
00:18:12,861 --> 00:18:14,661
Harkey explained why.

474
00:18:14,841 --> 00:18:17,600
A tall, flat front strikes a person

475
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:19,177
higher on the torso,

476
00:18:19,177 --> 00:18:21,542
pushing them forward and down,

477
00:18:21,542 --> 00:18:24,696
which often causes more severe injuries,

478
00:18:24,696 --> 00:18:26,509
frequently to the head.

479
00:18:26,858 --> 00:18:28,333
Here is the twist.

480
00:18:28,513 --> 00:18:31,218
Trucks did not get dangerous by accident.

481
00:18:31,398 --> 00:18:33,965
They got bigger because buyers wanted them

482
00:18:33,965 --> 00:18:34,393
bigger.

483
00:18:34,573 --> 00:18:35,839
According to IIHS,

484
00:18:35,839 --> 00:18:38,583
over the past three decades the average

485
00:18:38,583 --> 00:18:41,959
American passenger vehicle has become about four

486
00:18:41,959 --> 00:18:44,209
inches wider, ten inches longer,

487
00:18:44,209 --> 00:18:45,616
eight inches taller,

488
00:18:45,616 --> 00:18:47,867
and one thousand pounds heavier.

489
00:18:48,047 --> 00:18:51,132
And NPR reported that pedestrian deaths are

490
00:18:51,132 --> 00:18:53,643
at their highest level in more than

491
00:18:53,643 --> 00:18:56,513
forty years, up more than eighty percent

492
00:18:56,513 --> 00:18:58,020
since twenty oh nine.

493
00:18:58,369 --> 00:19:00,194
So what can a buyer do about

494
00:19:00,194 --> 00:19:00,390
it?

495
00:19:00,570 --> 00:19:03,585
Look at the pedestrian crash prevention rating,

496
00:19:03,585 --> 00:19:06,344
which measures whether the truck brakes for

497
00:19:06,344 --> 00:19:07,756
people in front of it.

498
00:19:07,936 --> 00:19:11,319
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk,

499
00:19:11,319 --> 00:19:13,921
the F-150 and Ram scored good,

500
00:19:13,921 --> 00:19:17,477
while the Silverado and the Tundra scored

501
00:19:17,477 --> 00:19:18,432
acceptable.

502
00:19:18,612 --> 00:19:21,510
Front cameras and parking sensors help in

503
00:19:21,510 --> 00:19:22,571
a driveway too.

504
00:19:22,751 --> 00:19:24,889
A tall truck will always have a

505
00:19:24,889 --> 00:19:26,268
blind zone in front.

506
00:19:26,448 --> 00:19:29,130
The technology is how you shrink it.

507
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,610
So what does all of this tell

508
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:32,638
a truck buyer?

509
00:19:32,818 --> 00:19:36,191
Big pickups protect their front-seat occupants very

510
00:19:36,191 --> 00:19:38,705
well, and most have strong structures.

511
00:19:38,885 --> 00:19:40,727
But in twenty twenty-six,

512
00:19:40,727 --> 00:19:41,759
the back seat,

513
00:19:41,759 --> 00:19:45,296
the headlights, and the newest automatic braking

514
00:19:45,296 --> 00:19:47,801
test are where trucks fall behind.

515
00:19:47,981 --> 00:19:50,439
And those are exactly the things that

516
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:53,162
ads, dealers and spec sheets almost never

517
00:19:53,162 --> 00:19:53,693
mention.

518
00:19:54,043 --> 00:19:55,971
And here is the final twist.

519
00:19:56,151 --> 00:19:58,631
The two pickups that won awards are

520
00:19:58,631 --> 00:20:01,819
the one with the most traditional reputation,

521
00:20:01,819 --> 00:20:03,095
the Toyota Tundra,

522
00:20:03,095 --> 00:20:05,787
and the one with the least traditional

523
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:07,842
design, the Tesla Cybertruck.

524
00:20:08,022 --> 00:20:10,976
The three best-selling American trucks,

525
00:20:10,976 --> 00:20:13,172
the ones on every dealer lot,

526
00:20:13,172 --> 00:20:14,384
did not qualify.

527
00:20:14,564 --> 00:20:18,217
Popularity and safety ratings are two completely

528
00:20:18,217 --> 00:20:19,510
different things.

529
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:22,211
So here is your safety checklist for

530
00:20:22,211 --> 00:20:23,518
twenty twenty-seven.

531
00:20:23,698 --> 00:20:25,869
One, look up the IIHS ratings for

532
00:20:25,869 --> 00:20:28,237
the exact cab style and model years.

533
00:20:28,417 --> 00:20:30,764
Two, if anyone rides in the back,

534
00:20:30,764 --> 00:20:33,182
check the moderate overlap rating,

535
00:20:33,182 --> 00:20:35,743
and specifically the rear passenger.

536
00:20:35,923 --> 00:20:38,628
Three, check the headlight rating for your

537
00:20:38,628 --> 00:20:39,336
exact trim.

538
00:20:39,516 --> 00:20:43,298
Four, confirm front crash prevention is standard,

539
00:20:43,298 --> 00:20:46,308
and check its vehicle-to-vehicle score.

540
00:20:46,488 --> 00:20:49,009
Five, think about who walks around your

541
00:20:49,009 --> 00:20:51,852
truck, especially children in your driveway.

542
00:20:52,201 --> 00:20:54,690
We put this checklist into the Twenty

543
00:20:54,690 --> 00:20:56,909
Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide,

544
00:20:56,909 --> 00:20:59,465
along with every other check from this

545
00:20:59,465 --> 00:21:00,003
channel.

546
00:21:00,183 --> 00:21:02,298
The link is in the description and

547
00:21:02,298 --> 00:21:03,666
in the pinned comment.

548
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:05,003
If this helped,

549
00:21:05,003 --> 00:21:08,240
subscribe, because next we answer how long

550
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,705
trucks really last,

551
00:21:09,705 --> 00:21:11,555
using real mileage data.

552
00:21:11,735 --> 00:21:13,405
And tell us in the comments,

553
00:21:13,405 --> 00:21:15,671
did any of these ratings surprise you?

554
00:21:15,851 --> 00:21:17,070
Thanks for watching.
